-- Section 204: payments to States. Layer 1: the law, objectively.
-- The relation: the State holds a claim against the United States for one-half of the sharable
-- compensation it pays individuals under the State law; the Secretary of Labor estimates and
-- certifies the sums, and the Secretary of the Treasury pays them. The individual is not a party
-- to this relation. It matters to the individual only because section 202(a)(6) and these
-- exclusions decide which payments the State may recover, and so which it can afford to make.
-- All figures of money are in dollars. Where a week's payment is partly shared, the shared part
-- is computed week by week, in the order of the Act: the exclusions of (a)(2), the caps of (b) and
-- (c), one-half under (a)(1), the reduction of (a)(3).
-- out of text: section 233 of the Trade Act of 1974; section 3306(c)(7) of the Internal Revenue
-- Code (services whose wages reduce the sum); any Federal law that reimburses the State for the
-- compensation; the State law's benefit structure, first-week rule and rounding.

§ `Section 204: payments to States`

§§ `204(a)(2): compensation for which no payment is made`

-- src:109 | No payment shall be made to any State under this subsection in respect of compensation (A) for which the State is entitled to reimbursement under the provisions of any Federal law other than this Act
-- src:109 | (B) paid for the first week in an individual’s eligibility period for which extended compensation or sharable regular compensation is paid, if the State law of such State provides for payment (at any time or under any circumstances) of regular compensation to an individual for his first week of otherwise compensable unemployment
-- src:109 | (C) paid for any week with respect to which such benefits are not payable by reason of section 233(d) [now 233(c)] of the Trade Act of 1974 [19 U.S.C. 2293(c)]
@ref s 204(a)(2)(A), (B), (C) (src:109)
GIVEN paid IS A `Compensation paid for a week`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no payment is made to the State in respect of the compensation under section 204(a)(2)(A), (B) or (C)` paid MEANS
        paid's `the State is entitled to reimbursement under a Federal law other than this title`
    OR  (    paid's `first week in the eligibility period for which extended compensation or sharable regular compensation is paid`
         AND paid's `the State law provides for payment of regular compensation for a first week of otherwise compensable unemployment`)
    OR  paid's `benefits are not payable for the week by reason of section 233 of the Trade Act of 1974`

-- src:109 | (D) paid to an individual with respect to a week of unemployment to the extent that such amount exceeds the amount of such compensation which would be paid to such individual if such State had a benefit structure which provided that the amount of compensation otherwise payable to any individual for any week shall be rounded (if not a full dollar amount) to the nearest lower full dollar amount.
@ref s 204(a)(2)(D) (src:109)
GIVEN paid IS A `Compensation paid for a week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the compensation counted for the week after section 204(a)(2)` paid MEANS
    IF `no payment is made to the State in respect of the compensation under section 204(a)(2)(A), (B) or (C)` paid
    THEN 0
    ELSE `the lesser of two amounts`
            (paid's `amount paid for the week`)
            (paid's `amount that would be paid for the week if the State rounded down to the nearest lower full dollar`)

§§ `204(b): sharable extended compensation`

-- src:111 | “(b) [Sharable Extended Compensation] For purposes of subsection (a)(1)(A), extended compensation paid to an individual for weeks of unemployment in such individual’s eligibility period is sharable extended compensation to the extent that the aggregate extended compensation paid to such individual with respect to any benefit year does not exceed the smallest of the amounts referred to in subparagraphs (A), (B), and (C) of section 202(b)(1).
@ref s 204(b) (src:111)
GIVEN paid IS A `Compensation paid for a week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sharable extended compensation for the week` paid MEANS
    IF (paid's `kind of compensation paid` EQUALS `extended compensation`) AND paid's `the week is in the individual's eligibility period`
    THEN `the lesser of two amounts` `the compensation counted this week` `the room left under the smallest amount`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the compensation counted this week` MEANS `the compensation counted for the week after section 204(a)(2)` paid
        `the room left under the smallest amount` MEANS
            `the greater of two amounts` 0
                (paid's `smallest of the amounts in section 202(b)(1)(A), (B) and (C)` MINUS paid's `extended compensation paid to the individual earlier in the benefit year`)

§§ `204(c): sharable regular compensation`

-- src:113 | “(1) if such week is in such individual’s eligibility period (determined under section 203(c)), and
-- src:114 | “(2) to the extent that the sum of such compensation, plus the regular compensation paid (or deemed paid) to him with respect to prior weeks of unemployment in the benefit year, exceeds twenty-six times (and does not exceed thirty-nine, forty-six in any case where section 202(b)(3)(A) applies[,] times) the average weekly benefit amount (including allowances for dependents) for weeks of total unemployment payable to such individual under the State law in such benefit year.
@ref s 204(c)(1) and (2) (src:113-114)
GIVEN paid IS A `Compensation paid for a week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sharable regular compensation for the week` paid MEANS
    IF (paid's `kind of compensation paid` EQUALS `regular compensation`) AND paid's `the week is in the individual's eligibility period`
    THEN `the greater of two amounts` 0 `the part of the running total inside the band`
    ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the regular compensation paid before the week` MEANS
            paid's `regular compensation paid or deemed paid to the individual for prior weeks in the benefit year`
        `the running total with this week` MEANS
            `the regular compensation paid before the week` PLUS `the compensation counted for the week after section 204(a)(2)` paid
        `the lower limit of the band` MEANS
            26 TIMES paid's `average weekly benefit amount, including allowances for dependents, for weeks of total unemployment`
        `the part of the running total inside the band` MEANS
            (`the lesser of two amounts` `the running total with this week` (`the upper limit of the sharable regular compensation band` paid))
                MINUS (`the greater of two amounts` `the regular compensation paid before the week` `the lower limit of the band`)

-- "exceeds twenty-six times (and does not exceed thirty-nine, forty-six in any case where section
-- 202(b)(3)(A) applies[,] times) the average weekly benefit amount": the band is 26 to 39 times,
-- or 26 to 46 times where section 202(b)(3)(A) applies (fork register).
-- src:114 | “(2) to the extent that the sum of such compensation, plus the regular compensation paid (or deemed paid) to him with respect to prior weeks of unemployment in the benefit year, exceeds twenty-six times (and does not exceed thirty-nine, forty-six in any case where section 202(b)(3)(A) applies[,] times) the average weekly benefit amount (including allowances for dependents) for weeks of total unemployment payable to such individual under the State law in such benefit year.
@ref s 204(c)(2) (src:114)
GIVEN paid IS A `Compensation paid for a week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the upper limit of the sharable regular compensation band` paid MEANS
    (IF paid's `section 202(b)(3)(A) applies to the week` THEN 46 ELSE 39)
        TIMES paid's `average weekly benefit amount, including allowances for dependents, for weeks of total unemployment`

§§ `204(a)(3): wages for services to which section 3306(c)(7) applies`

-- src:110 | “(3) The amount which, but for this paragraph, would be payable under this subsection to any State in respect of any compensation paid to an individual whose base period wages include wages for services to which section 3306(c)(7) of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 applies shall be reduced by an amount which bears the same ratio to the amount which, but for this paragraph, would be payable under this subsection to such State in respect of such compensation as the amount of the base period wages attributable to such services bears to the total amount of the base period wages.
@ref s 204(a)(3) (src:110)
GIVEN paid IS A `Compensation paid for a week`
      `the amount payable but for this paragraph` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount payable after the reduction in section 204(a)(3)` paid `the amount payable but for this paragraph` MEANS
    IF paid's `total base period wages` GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the amount payable but for this paragraph`
            MINUS (`the amount payable but for this paragraph`
                   TIMES (paid's `base period wages attributable to services to which section 3306(c)(7) of the Internal Revenue Code applies` DIVIDED BY paid's `total base period wages`))
    ELSE `the amount payable but for this paragraph`

§§ `204(a)(1): one-half of the sharable compensation`

-- src:105 | “(a) [Amount Payable] (1) There shall be paid to each State an amount equal to one-half of the sum of—
-- src:106 | “(A) the sharable extended compensation, and
-- src:107 | “(B) the sharable regular compensation,
-- src:108 | paid to individuals under the State law.
@ref s 204(a)(1) (src:105-108)
GIVEN paid IS A `Compensation paid for a week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount payable to the State for the week but for section 204(a)(3)` paid MEANS
    (`the sharable extended compensation for the week` paid PLUS `the sharable regular compensation for the week` paid) DIVIDED BY 2

-- src:105 | “(a) [Amount Payable] (1) There shall be paid to each State an amount equal to one-half of the sum of—
-- src:106 | “(A) the sharable extended compensation, and
-- src:107 | “(B) the sharable regular compensation,
-- src:108 | paid to individuals under the State law.
-- src:109 | “(2) No payment shall be made to any State under this subsection in respect of compensation (A) for which the State is entitled to reimbursement under the provisions of any Federal law other than this Act, (B) paid for the first week in an individual’s eligibility period for which extended compensation or sharable regular compensation is paid, if the State law of such State provides for payment (at any time or under any circumstances) of regular compensation to an individual for his first week of otherwise compensable unemployment, (C) paid for any week with respect to which such benefits are not payable by reason of section 233(d) [now 233(c)] of the Trade Act of 1974 [19 U.S.C. 2293(c)], or (D) paid to an individual with respect to a week of unemployment to the extent that such amount exceeds the amount of such compensation which would be paid to such individual if such State had a benefit structure which provided that the amount of compensation otherwise payable to any individual for any week shall be rounded (if not a full dollar amount) to the nearest lower full dollar amount.
-- src:110 | “(3) The amount which, but for this paragraph, would be payable under this subsection to any State in respect of any compensation paid to an individual whose base period wages include wages for services to which section 3306(c)(7) of the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 applies shall be reduced by an amount which bears the same ratio to the amount which, but for this paragraph, would be payable under this subsection to such State in respect of such compensation as the amount of the base period wages attributable to such services bears to the total amount of the base period wages.
@ref s 204(a) (src:105-110)
GIVEN paid IS A `Compensation paid for a week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount payable to the State for the week` paid MEANS
    `the amount payable after the reduction in section 204(a)(3)` paid (`the amount payable to the State for the week but for section 204(a)(3)` paid)

-- Section 204 applies only to the weeks that section 207 reaches.
-- src:138 | “(2) section 204 shall apply only with respect to weeks of unemployment beginning after December 31, 1971.
@ref s 207(a)(2), (b)(3) and s 204(a) (src:138)
GIVEN week IS A DATE
      `the week is in an extended benefit period determined under a State law provision described in section 207(b)(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      paid IS A `Compensation paid for a week`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount payable to the State for the week of unemployment` week `the week is in an extended benefit period determined under a State law provision described in section 207(b)(1)` paid MEANS
    IF `section 204 applies to the week of unemployment` week `the week is in an extended benefit period determined under a State law provision described in section 207(b)(1)`
    THEN `the amount payable to the State for the week` paid
    ELSE 0

§§ `204(d): payment on a calendar month basis`

-- src:115 | There shall be paid to each State either in advance or by way of reimbursement, as may be determined by the Secretary, such sum as the Secretary estimates the State will be entitled to receive under this title for each calendar month, reduced or increased, as the case may be, by any sum by which the Secretary finds that his estimates for any prior calendar month were greater or less than the amounts which should have been paid to the State.
@ref s 204(d) (src:115)
GIVEN `the sum the Secretary estimates the State will be entitled to receive for the calendar month` IS A NUMBER
      `the sum by which prior months' estimates were greater than the amounts which should have been paid, or minus the sum by which they were less` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum to be paid to the State for the calendar month` `the sum the Secretary estimates the State will be entitled to receive for the calendar month` `the sum by which prior months' estimates were greater than the amounts which should have been paid, or minus the sum by which they were less` MEANS
    `the sum the Secretary estimates the State will be entitled to receive for the calendar month`
        MINUS `the sum by which prior months' estimates were greater than the amounts which should have been paid, or minus the sum by which they were less`

§§ `204(e): certification and payment`

-- src:116 | “(e) [Certification] The Secretary shall from time to time certify to the Secretary of the Treasury for payment to each State the sums payable to such State under this section. The Secretary of the Treasury, prior to audit or settlement by the Government Accountability Office, shall make payment to the State in accordance with such certification, by transfers from the extended unemployment compensation account to the account of such State in the Unemployment Trust Fund.
@ref s 204(e) (src:116)
GIVETH A Party
`the party who certifies the sums payable to each State` MEANS `the Secretary of Labor`

-- src:116 | “(e) [Certification] The Secretary shall from time to time certify to the Secretary of the Treasury for payment to each State the sums payable to such State under this section. The Secretary of the Treasury, prior to audit or settlement by the Government Accountability Office, shall make payment to the State in accordance with such certification, by transfers from the extended unemployment compensation account to the account of such State in the Unemployment Trust Fund.
@ref s 204(e) (src:116)
GIVETH A Party
`the party who pays each State the certified sums` MEANS `the Secretary of the Treasury`

-- src:116 | The Secretary of the Treasury, prior to audit or settlement by the Government Accountability Office, shall make payment to the State in accordance with such certification
@ref s 204(e) (src:116)
GIVEN `the sum the Secretary of Labor certified as payable to the State` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the sum the Secretary of the Treasury must pay the State` `the sum the Secretary of Labor certified as payable to the State` MEANS
    `the sum the Secretary of Labor certified as payable to the State`
